extends Node
## AudioDirector (autoload, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md section 33): every sound the game makes.
##
## The simulation never makes sound; the battle controller calls `on_event(e)` once for every timeline
## event it plays, and this node maps the event to a sound. Nothing here influences the game.
##
## Buses (default_bus_layout.tres): Master -> SFX, UI, Music. The settings screen's "Sound effects" volume and
## on/off drive the SFX bus, "UI sounds" on/off the UI bus (which also follows the effects volume and goes
## silent with effects off), "Music" volume and on/off the Music bus. They live in ShowSettings and are
## re-applied whenever they change (see `apply_settings`).
##
## Sounds are 16-bit mono WAVs generated by tools/sfx/gen_sfx.py (presets in tools/sfx/presets.json) and are
## preloaded once below. Playback uses fixed pools of AudioStreamPlayer nodes: MAX_VOICES for effects (the
## quietest/oldest voice is stolen when a more important sound arrives, and a new sound that is less
## important than everything playing is dropped), UI_VOICES for UI sounds, plus one node each for the
## two loops (well hum, fire crackle) and the music. No node or stream is created while playing.
## Pitch is jittered by +-PITCH_JITTER so repeated sounds do not machine-gun. Playback speed 2x only shortens
## the minimum gap between equal sounds (more overlap), it never changes pitch.
##
## HOW TO ADD MUSIC: drop an OGG (Vorbis) file into game/assets/music/, add a line to MUSIC_TRACKS below, e.g.
##     "menu": "res://assets/music/menu.ogg",
## and call AudioDirector.play_music("menu") where it should start (AudioDirector.stop_music() to end it).
## In the OGG's Import dock tick "Loop" so it repeats. The Music bus and the Settings "Music" volume/switch
## already work, so no other change is needed. (There is no track yet, so play_music() is a silent no-op.)

## Effect volume (dB, before the SFX bus), priority (1-10: how important when the pool is full) and the
## minimum gap in milliseconds between two plays of the same sound.
const SOUNDS: Dictionary = {
